<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<task id="021" project="spaarkeai-mcp-bff-api-r1">
  <metadata>
    <title>A10 auth on /mcp, tool policies and route guard</title>
    <phase>B MCP host and tools</phase>
    <gate>after 020</gate>
    <status>not-started</status>
    <rigor>FULL</rigor>
    <rigor-reason>Tags include auth and bff-api; modifies auth configuration, endpoints and ArchTests (.cs)</rigor-reason>
    <model-tier>opus</model-tier>
    <model-tier-reason>Security/auth-sensitive (tags auth, authorization): A10 token acceptance and refusal before any tool runs, and the route-guard ratchet</model-tier-reason>
    <effort>high</effort>
    <parallel-group>E</parallel-group>
    <parallel-safe>true</parallel-safe>
    <parallel-reason>Owns AuthorizationModule.cs, Api/Mcp/McpEndpoints.cs, Api/Mcp/McpToolAuthorization.cs and RouteAuthorizationGuardTests.cs in its wave; 014 and 016 touch none</parallel-reason>
    <deps>020</deps>
    <tags>bff-api, auth, authorization, endpoints, integration-test, testing</tags>
    <estimated-effort>4-6 hours</estimated-effort>
  </metadata>

  <prompt>Make /mcp/* accept only ADR-028 A10 tokens (Spaarke-tenant authority, aud = BFF, scope user_impersonation, systemuser callers), refuse CIAM and A9 home-directory tokens server-side before any tool runs, add per-tool authorization policies (B-7), and extend RouteAuthorizationGuardTests to MapMcp with tool-annotation checks (B-8), meeting unified-access-control-r2's four checks.</prompt>
  <role>SPAARKE platform developer. Follow ADRs strictly. Expert in ASP.NET Core JWT bearer authentication, authorization policies and architecture tests.</role>
  <goal>/mcp/* enforces A10 with refusals before any tool runs; tools carry per-tool policies that reuse existing policies; the ArchTest guard covers MapMcp with must-fire and must-not-fire controls and checks every tool's ReadOnly annotation and title; uac-r2's four checks pass.</goal>

  <context>
    <background>Spec FR-02 and its review conditions; ADR-028 A10; design §6 and §8 B-7, B-8. AuthorizationModule.cs: ApplyFallbackPolicy L914, AuthSchemes.Ciam and WorkforceHome. RouteAuthorizationGuardTests recognises Map{Verb}, MapMethods and MapHealthChecks today (verb list ~L2642).</background>
    <relevant-files>
      <file role="modify">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Infrastructure/DI/AuthorizationModule.cs (ONLY if A10 needs a scheme change: ApplyFallbackPolicy L914; AuthSchemes.Ciam / WorkforceHome)</file>
      <file role="modify">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Api/Mcp/McpEndpoints.cs (auth metadata, challenge)</file>
      <file role="new">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Api/Mcp/McpToolAuthorization.cs (AddAuthorizationFilters + per-tool [Authorize(Policy = …)] wiring)</file>
      <file role="modify">tests/Spaarke.ArchTests/RouteAuthorizationGuardTests.cs (MapMcp in the scanned verbs ~L2642; tool ReadOnly/title check; no AI-internal types in tools)</file>
      <file role="new">tests/integration/auth/Mcp/McpAuthTests.cs</file>
      <file role="canonical-reference">.claude/adr/ADR-028-spaarke-auth-architecture.md (A10)</file>
      <file role="canonical-reference">PnP mcp-cs-customers-secure-server (auth pattern, SDK 1.2.0 → 2.3.1; external sample, MIT)</file>
    </relevant-files>
    <dependencies>
      <dependency task="020" status="pending">The /mcp/{area} host and test host</dependency>
    </dependencies>
  </context>

  <constraints>
    <constraint source="ADR-028">/mcp/* accepts only tokens from the Spaarke-tenant authority with aud = the BFF app and scope user_impersonation that resolve to a systemuser; CIAM and A9 home-directory tokens are refused with 401 server-side before any tool runs (A10).</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-028">No code path in this task passes the caller's token downstream to a client or logs it or its claims; a failed OBO never falls back to app-only, and any app-only read applies the caller's own record-access check (FR-02).</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-008">/mcp/* falls under the authorization FallbackPolicy; no anonymous route is added (only /healthz and /ping stay anonymous); per-tool policies reuse existing named policies and never ExternalCollaboration (B-7).</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">The RouteAuthorizationGuardTests extension ships with a must-fire control (an unauthenticated MapMcp in fixture source fails) and a must-not-fire control, and a seeding proof is recorded (security guard).</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">unified-access-control-r2 reviews the diff against FR-02's four checks before merge, and two adversarial-reviewer passes are recorded (root CLAUDE.md §8.5).</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-015">Every log statement or telemetry property this task adds records identifiers, sizes, timings and outcome/reason codes only: no bearer token, claim value, record text or tool argument (NFR-05).</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-029">Every change this task makes under src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/ is listed in the PR with a Placement Justification that cites .claude/constraints/bff-extensions.md (source text: spec.md 'Placement Justification'), and the PR records the publish-size delta against a fresh master build per .claude/constraints/azure-deployment.md 'BFF Publish-Size Per-Task Verification Rule': a delta of +5 MB or more needs explicit justification, a total of 55 MB or more triggers architecture review, and the total must stay at or under 60 MB (hard stop). No new HIGH CVE (dotnet list package --vulnerable --include-transitive).</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-038">Every test this task adds lives on a KEEP path (tests/integration/{auth,contract,regression,data-mutation}/** or tests/unit/domain/**), mocks only at module boundaries, and uses no Mock&lt;HttpMessageHandler&gt; or Mock&lt;IServiceClient&gt;.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">Any defect found and not fixed in this task is filed with /project-defer-issue-tracking (notes/defer-issues.md AND a GitHub issue), never one without the other (project CLAUDE.md §2).</constraint>
  </constraints>

  <knowledge>
    <files>
      <file>.claude/constraints/api.md</file>
