  </knowledge>

  <steps mode="directional">
    <step order="1">Read ADR-028 A10, AuthorizationModule.cs (schemes, ApplyFallbackPolicy L914) and the T5 claim evidence in notes/phase0-registration-facts.md.</step>
    <step order="2">Configure /mcp/* to the default workforce scheme with explicit refusal of CIAM and A9 home-directory tokens before endpoint execution; change AuthorizationModule.cs only if the existing schemes cannot express A10.</step>
    <step order="3">Emit a 401 with a WWW-Authenticate challenge per the MCP authorization spec (escalation below if it needs an anonymous metadata route).</step>
    <step order="4">Add McpToolAuthorization: AddAuthorizationFilters and per-tool policies reusing existing policies.</step>
    <step order="5">Extend RouteAuthorizationGuardTests: MapMcp scanned; every [McpServerTool] has explicit ReadOnly and Title; no tool constructor injects a Services/Ai/** type; must-fire, must-not-fire and the seeding proof.</step>
    <step order="6">Write McpAuthTests covering the acceptance criteria; run auth, contract and ArchTests suites.</step>
    <step order="7">Request unified-access-control-r2 review and two adversarial-reviewer passes; measure the publish-size delta.</step>
    <step order="8">Update TASK-INDEX.md: change this task's status cell to `✅ [done]` (the bracketed ASCII token is mandatory, the emoji alone is not greppable: task-create Step 5, FAILURE-MODES G-16), set the POML &lt;status&gt; to completed, and run pwsh scripts/check-task-status-drift.ps1</step>
    <step order="9">If any deviations from plan, document in projects/spaarkeai-mcp-bff-api-r1/notes/ (decisions go to notes/decisions.md)</step>
  </steps>

  <escalation>
    <trigger>If the WWW-Authenticate challenge needs an anonymous protected-resource-metadata route (RFC 9728 /.well-known/oauth-protected-resource), STOP and escalate with options: FR-02 allows no anonymous route other than /healthz and /ping (root CLAUDE.md §9).</trigger>
    <trigger>If A10 cannot be expressed without changing an existing scheme used by other planes, STOP and escalate to the owner and unified-access-control-r2 before editing AuthorizationModule.cs.</trigger>
    <trigger>If any existing auth test changes expected behaviour, STOP (AP-9).</trigger>
  </escalation>

  <justification>
    <existing>AuthorizationModule.cs schemes and FallbackPolicy (L914); existing named policies; RouteAuthorizationGuardTests.cs (no MapMcp coverage today).</existing>
    <extension>Yes for policies and the guard: per-tool policies reuse existing ones and the guard is extended, not replaced; McpToolAuthorization.cs is new only because endpoint filters (ADR-008) do not reach MCP tools.</extension>
    <cost-of-doing-nothing>Without it, CIAM or A9 tokens could reach tools, checks held in endpoint filters would not apply to tools, and a new unauthenticated MCP route would be invisible to the ratchet.</cost-of-doing-nothing>
  </justification>

  <tools>
    <tool name="dotnet">Build and test .NET projects (dotnet build src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/, dotnet test)</tool>
    <tool name="terminal">Run shell commands</tool>
  </tools>

  <outputs>
    <output type="code">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Api/Mcp/McpToolAuthorization.cs</output>
    <output type="code">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Api/Mcp/McpEndpoints.cs</output>
    <output type="test">tests/integration/auth/Mcp/McpAuthTests.cs</output>
    <output type="test">tests/Spaarke.ArchTests/RouteAuthorizationGuardTests.cs</output>
  </outputs>

  <acceptance-criteria>
    <criterion testable="true">Negative: an anonymous call to /mcp/legal-operations returns 401 with a WWW-Authenticate challenge.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Negative: a CIAM token returns 401 and an A9 home-directory token returns 401, each with the probe tool's invocation counter at 0 (refused before any tool runs).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Negative: a valid token that resolves to no systemuser gets the existing UserContextRequired refusal as an isError result.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Negative: when OBO fails, the tool returns an isError result and the app-only client is never invoked (spy assertion).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">A valid A10 token for a licensed user runs the probe tool as that caller.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">/mcp/* falls under the FallbackPolicy: a test endpoint mapped under /mcp without explicit auth still returns 401.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">RouteAuthorizationGuardTests: an unauthenticated MapMcp fixture fails (must-fire), an authenticated one passes (must-not-fire), and the seeding proof is recorded.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">The guard fails a fixture tool without an explicit ReadOnly annotation or title, and a fixture tool injecting a Services/Ai type.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">No MCP endpoint or tool carries the ExternalCollaboration policy (arch test); grep shows no token or claim value logged.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">The PR records unified-access-control-r2's review of the four checks, two adversarial passes, and the publish-size delta (at or under 60 MB, no new HIGH CVE).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Test scope: cover the stated contract plus the edge cases named in these criteria; anything beyond that needs a one-line justification in the task notes.</criterion>
  </acceptance-criteria>

  <notes>uac-r2's four checks (naming note §2): FallbackPolicy covers /mcp/*; must-fire guard test on an unauthenticated /mcp/{area}; CIAM and A9 refused server-side before any tool runs, tested; no app-only fallback on failed OBO.</notes>

  <execution>
    <skill>.claude/skills/task-execute/SKILL.md</skill>
    <protocol>Before starting, load all files listed in &lt;knowledge&gt;&lt;files&gt;. Follow task-execute for the pre-execution checklist.</protocol>
  </execution>
</task>
